{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Elohim came to Laban the Aramean.</b> Prior to 'and he overtook him.' Its meaning: Elohim had already come, and I have already shown you many like it, and HaShem came for Jacob's honor." "<b>From good to bad.</b> That you should think it is good for him — do not speak to him to turn him back."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:34.634461870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}